<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="site-header">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Seer Frights home"><span>SEER</span><strong>FRIGHTS</strong></a>
  <button class="menu-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav">Menu</button>
  <nav id="main-nav" class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
    <a class="active" href="/">Home</a>
    <a href="/books/">Books</a>
    <a href="/about/">About</a>
  </nav>
</header>
<main id="main">
<section class="home-hero">
  <img src="/images/hero-home.webp" alt="Moonlit swamp boardwalk beside a cornfield and twisted moss-covered tree" fetchpriority="high">
  <div class="shell hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Middle-grade horror · Ages 8+ · By B. Carter</p>
    <h1>SEER FRIGHTS</h1>
    <p class="tagline">You should be scared.</p>
    <p class="lede">Standalone scary books for kids who finished Goosebumps and want more of <em>exactly</em> that — and for the grown-ups who grew up on it. Every chapter ends on a scare. Half of them are fake. The other half are real — and you’ll never know which until you turn the page.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-green" href="/books/">See the books ›</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/books/dont-go-into-the-swamp/">Start with Book 1</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-note">“One rule: don’t trust the quiet chapters.”</div>
</section>

<section class="parchment">
  <div class="home-intro">
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">The deal</p>
      <h2>You scream. You laugh. Often on the same page.</h2>
      <p>Every Seer Frights book runs the same engine — standalone, fast, funny, and built to make you turn one more page.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-dark" href="/about/">About the series ›</a></p>
    </article>
    <article><div class="intro-icon">1</div><h3>Every chapter ends on a scare.</h3><p>A hand grabs. A face appears. You have to turn the page.</p></article>
    <article><div class="intro-icon">2</div><h3>Half the scares are fake.</h3><p>It was the cat. The wind. Your sibling. Until it wasn’t.</p></article>
    <article><div class="intro-icon">3</div><h3>The last page is the proof.</h3><p>No “maybe it was nothing.” The monster was real all along.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Newest scare</p>
      <h2>THE HOUSE THAT WASN’T THERE</h2>
      <p>BOOK 5 · AVAILABLE NOW</p>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/books/the-house-that-wasnt-there/">View Book 5 ›</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="book-showcase">
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span> THE BOOKS <span>✦</span></div>
  <div class="cover-row"><a class="cover-link" href="/books/dont-go-into-the-swamp/">
          <img src="/images/cover-dont-go-into-the-swamp-front.jpg" alt="Don’t Go into the Swamp cover" loading="lazy">
          <span>1. DON’T GO INTO THE SWAMP</span>
        </a><a class="cover-link" href="/books/the-scarecrows-know-your-name/">
          <img src="/images/cover-the-scarecrows-know-your-name-front.jpg" alt="The Scarecrows Know Your Name cover" loading="lazy">
          <span>2. THE SCARECROWS KNOW YOUR NAME</span>
        </a><a class="cover-link" href="/books/the-mark-spreads/">
          <img src="/images/cover-the-mark-spreads-front.jpg" alt="The Mark Spreads cover" loading="lazy">
          <span>3. THE MARK SPREADS</span>
        </a><a class="cover-link" href="/books/welcome-to-camp-sunny-pines/">
          <img src="/images/cover-welcome-to-camp-sunny-pines-front.jpg" alt="Welcome to Camp Sunny Pines cover" loading="lazy">
          <span>4. WELCOME TO CAMP SUNNY PINES</span>
        </a><a class="cover-link" href="/books/the-house-that-wasnt-there/">
          <img src="/images/cover-the-house-that-wasnt-there-front.jpg" alt="The House That Wasn’t There cover" loading="lazy">
          <span>5. THE HOUSE THAT WASN’T THERE</span>
        </a></div>
  
</section>

<section class="paper-section">
  <div class="shell split-feature">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Scary, not scarring</p>
      <h2>Made for the flashlight-under-the-covers crowd.</h2>
      <p>An 8-year-old can finish one and still sleep. A 12-year-old gets the better jokes. And the adult reading over their shoulder gets pulled right back to being ten.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.4rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-green" href="/books/dont-go-into-the-swamp/">Start with Book 1 ›</a>
        <a class="btn btn-paper" href="/books/">Browse all books</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split-art">
      <img src="/images/cover-dont-go-into-the-swamp-front.jpg" alt="Don't Go into the Swamp — Seer Frights Book 1 cover" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="night-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">What it is · what it isn’t</p>
      <h2>Quick scares. Real laughs. No gore.</h2>
      <p>Same engine, every age — you just bring your own flashlight.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature-box"><div class="big-icon">✓</div><h3>Creepy &amp; funny</h3><p>Real dread, real laughs. Gross-out gags and bickering siblings keep it fun.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-box"><div class="big-icon">✓</div><h3>Bloodless</h3><p>The scariest thing is a face in a window, never a wound. No gore.</p></article>
      <article class="feature-box"><div class="big-icon">✓</div><h3>Read in any order</h3><p>No homework. Pick any one cold — no recurring hero, no prior reading.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="paper-section">
  <div class="shell split-feature">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For the kid you used to be</p>
      <h2>Grown-ups, these are for you too.</h2>
      <p>If you read Goosebumps under the covers in the ’90s, you already know the feeling these books are built to give back. Read one yourself in a single sitting, or read it out loud to a kid and watch them refuse to let you stop. The scares are quick, the jokes land for both of you, and nobody’s too old to be scared of what’s in the swamp.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.4rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-green" href="/books/dont-go-into-the-swamp/">Start with Book 1 ›</a>
        <a class="btn btn-dark" href="https://seerwarns.com/books/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Want it darker? Seer Warns ›</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img src="/images/about-scene.webp" alt="Moonlit boardwalk and twisted tree in a spooky swamp" loading="lazy" style="border-radius:22px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>You should be scared.</h2>
    <p>One rule: don’t trust the quiet chapters.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-green" href="/books/">Browse all the books ›</a>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
